ic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=4-2=2.\n$$" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430412 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430408 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430412 1069 "q-85930" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430412 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430412 1071 "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430412 1072 #uuid "8f9a6384-39b0-554b-abeb-cd550f81dcbb" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430412 1074 "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((-3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )+2) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+5\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{A}^{3}+5A-2I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}(-{A}^{3}+5A-2I) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{2}+5I-2{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ 2{A}^{-1} & =5I-{A}^{2} \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430413 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430409 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430413 1069 "q-83394" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430413 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430413 1071 "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $\\text{tr}(A)=5$ and $\\text{det}(A)=9.$ Then, ${A}^{2}=$" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430413 1072 #uuid "ad99eb94-2179-5889-bd75-4a31770a9b01" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true] [17592186430413 1074 "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by \n\n$$\np(\\lambda )={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =5A-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534636 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-054199c2-5c89-5ffd-aead-8b50d8e9a898" 17592186430393 "answer-10181856-84b4-5e5e-8832-61fff9b19f1a" 17592186430394 "answer-1d65a687-0988-5518-994a-fcab04da4ebc" 17592186430395 "answer-3bde7c58-3f7c-5801-a261-da5680905d36" 17592186430396 "answer-4571d412-17c6-50e3-a5ad-250aba5664ee" 17592186430397 "answer-5d2122a1-0044-5550-a7b5-8c659f887082" 17592186430398 "answer-8506e219-a01e-50d0-9da2-c59e5aa39951" 17592186430399 "answer-8600afc6-a04f-52fd-8a1f-de56606615bb" 17592186430400 "answer-87762782-8da5-5b58-aec6-89ebd72a1767" 17592186430401 "answer-8e1bad79-e653-5c1b-8674-be7f593dc2d9" 17592186430402 "answer-97594f4f-bc35-5637-b1b2-7a025224b4ca" 17592186430403 "answer-cc2cc7ac-9a1b-526d-80a8-a3d8c973934c" 17592186430404 "answer-dfd0659a-536b-5595-88dd-23740eda781b" 17592186430405 "answer-f2683b79-0149-589d-9aee-43b4a2b94124" 17592186430406 "answer-f30920a8-926e-571d-b2ce-067087fbb78e" 17592186430407 "answer-field-34db680c-e9af-57f5-a298-893f9c03dc9c" 17592186430408 "answer-field-aa304203-2130-5c26-be53-cf5953cd34e5" 175